From: Zhyi <molishanguang@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] H28K: release RTL8211F reset with a U-Boot gpio-hog

The board-specific U-Boot never releases the RTL8211F reset: dwc_eth_qos's
PHY path only runs on a network command, and DWC_ETH_QOS_ROCKCHIP selects
DM_ETH_PHY, which compiles phy_gpio_reset() into a no-op stub. The reset
line (gpio4 RK_PC2) is pulled low at power-on, so Linux's first MDIO scan
cannot read the PHY ID and eth0 stays down ("MDIO device at address 1 is
missing", "cannot attach to PHY (-ENODEV)").

Drive the line high with a gpio-hog: the GPIO bank driver applies it at
probe time, before ethernet init and long before Linux starts, independent
of CONFIG_NET. The kernel DTS keeps the upstream phy-node reset-gpios; once
the PHY answers MDIO, Linux performs its own reset cycle.

---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3528-hinlink-h28k-u-boot.dtsi |    9 +++++++++
 configs/hinlink-h28k-rk3528_defconfig        |    1 +
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3528-hinlink-h28k-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3528-hinlink-h28k-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -9,3 +9,12 @@
 &vdd_logic {
 	regulator-init-microvolt = <900000>;
 };
+
+&gpio4 {
+	gmac1-rstn-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <RK_PC2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		output-low;
+		line-name = "gmac1-rstn";
+	};
+};
--- a/configs/hinlink-h28k-rk3528_defconfig
+++ b/configs/hinlink-h28k-rk3528_defconfig
@@ -34,3 +34,4 @@
 CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_GPIO=y
+CONFIG_GPIO_HOG=y
 CONFIG_LED=y
 CONFIG_LED_GPIO=y
